### Lifecycle control
# All lifecycle calls take only {"name": ...}. Run against a database that
# already exists (see 02-provision.http). Each returns 200.
#
# Status transitions:
#   create -> stopped
#   start  -> running
#   pause  -> paused
#   stop   -> stopped
#   delete -> gone (container + VOLUME destroyed)

@host = {{host}}

### Start — wake the database now (admin action; a client connecting does the same)
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "{{dbName}}" }

### Verify it is running
GET {{host}}/api/databases
Accept: application/json

### Pause — freeze processes via the Docker freezer
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/pause
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "{{dbName}}" }

### Stop — scale to zero now, without waiting for the idle timeout
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/stop
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "{{dbName}}" }

### Delete — DESTRUCTIVE: removes container AND volume. Data is gone.
POST {{host}}/api/{{engine}}/delete
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "{{dbName}}" }

### Confirm it is gone from the listing
GET {{host}}/api/databases
Accept: application/json
